 "note": "EIGH follow-ups (maintainer decisions F1, F2, F3 step 1, 2026-11-08). Before v0.1: no deprecated aliases. The machine contract FloatMachine.IsAccurate now extends the new arithmetic contract FloatMachine.IsArithAccurate (scalar fields and the matrix product); the Newton–Schulz, entrywise-rounding and deflation lemmas that use only arithmetic move to its namespace and assume it (the deflation theorems also take IsQRErr and IsNormalSampler). The SIGN and DEFLATE targets drop the conjunct asking for an accurate machine; the EIGH target's postcondition adds the weighted kernel count, and EP7 is stated with the shared OpKind.kernelWeight (EighWeight.kernelWeight moved). TT3 is restated over a floored semantics (IsFloorRelErrSem) and is no longer vacuous for binaryFloatSem, whose sqrt is now defined on nonnegative arguments. abs_sub_binaryFloatRound_le_mul_max is a duplicate of Computation.abs_sub_binaryFloatRound_le. Result ids are unchanged.",
